                "type": "text",
                "text": " - in order to resume an olake replication after a pause or after switching to a new machine, I need the state json.\nMy question is, how do you usually handle storing the state? I would've expected that it's stored in the iceberg sink, but turns out that isn't the case.\nRight now, I have a small script which downloads the state from S3 before the docker starts and uploads it after it finishes, but I'm not sure if this is optimal."
